{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.PerNucleonChannelDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.PerNucleonChannelDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.branchingFactorizationSigns","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.branchingFactorizationSigns","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L77-L91","doc":"Both channel sums are strictly negative for `q > 1` (`a, b < 0`),\nthe sign input to the branching factorization `a^Z · b^{N−1} · (a − b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.neutronChannelSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.neutronChannelSum","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L65-L75","doc":"**Neutron channel sum** `b = Σ_c G_N(c) = −3(q²−1)(q²+1)²/(4q³)`,\nstated conditionally on the standard-channel summed expectation\n`stdN` (computed in `def:typed-crossing-operator`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.protonChannelSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.protonChannelSum","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L48-L63","doc":"**Proton channel sum** `a = Σ_c G_P(c) = −h/2` (`h = q − q⁻¹`),\nstated conditionally on the standard-channel summed expectation\n`stdP = ⟨v₁|Δ₃|v₁⟩ + ⟨v₂|Δ₃|v₂⟩`.  The two standard-channel values\nare the quadratic-root eigendata of `T_{2,3} = σ₀σ₁σ₀` in the 2-dim\nstandard representation — not elementary in `q` — and are computed in\n`def:typed-crossing-operator`; this lemma verifies that, summed with\nthe explicit symmetric/alternating factors, they give `−h/2`\n(§3b-cond conditional pattern). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.gN_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.gN_alt","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L45-L46","doc":"Neutron alternating (sign) channel factor: `(−q) · (½[2]_q)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.gN_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.gN_sym","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L42-L43","doc":"Neutron symmetric (trivial) channel factor: `q⁻¹ · (½[2]_q)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.gP_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.gP_alt","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L39-L40","doc":"Proton alternating (sign) channel factor: `(−q⁻¹) · (½[2]_q)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.gP_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.gP_sym","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L35-L37","doc":"Proton symmetric (trivial) channel factor, explicit from the\nper-nucleon table: `q · (½[2]_q)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.qBracket2_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.qBracket2_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L29-L33","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical bracket.** The longhand `q + q⁻¹` is this site's\nbody and its proofs use it, so the consolidation is the identity, not an alias.\nConditional: the two agree away from `q − q⁻¹ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.qBracket2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.qBracket2","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L25-L26","doc":"The q-bracket `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel.sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel.sign","kind":"ctor","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L23-L23","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel.unconf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel.unconf","kind":"ctor","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel.conf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel.conf","kind":"ctor","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L21-L21","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel.triv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel.triv","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.KnotChannel","kind":"inductive","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean#L18-L23","doc":"The four channels from T_{2,3} eigendecomposition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}